#42796
"Obsidian Nest"
"Thick tendrils smother the room in a choking haze of sticky black webbing. 

Steep walls of obsidian rock line the chamber to the south and west, but the

heavy tendrils continue even onto the ceiling, hanging down to block the view

to the north and east.  This is some kind of nest, albeit a strange one.  A

low ring of piled obsidian stones forms a ring which closes in the southwest

corner.

"
